<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the signed macOS bundle
  (pyproject.toml: [[tool.pyappdist.targets]] name = "macos").

  Why this file exists (2026-08-12): the GHA-built, notarized .pkg crashed the
  moment background removal started (drop an image -> Start). The crash report
  (~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports/python3.12-*.ips) showed:

      exception:   EXC_BAD_ACCESS / SIGKILL (Code Signature Invalid)
      termination: namespace CODESIGNING, "Invalid Page"
      stack:       libllvmlite.dylib LLVMPY_TryAllocateExecutableMemory
                   -> llvm::sys::Memory::protectMappedMemory
                   -> sys_icache_invalidate  (worker thread "CompareWorker")

  numba/llvmlite JIT-compiles at runtime with plain mmap(PROT_EXEC) (no
  MAP_JIT). Notarization requires signing with the hardened runtime
  ("codesign - -options runtime"), which forbids unsigned executable memory:
  the kernel SIGKILLs the process on the first such page. Not a bug in the
  app - the hardened runtime working as designed, until the entitlements
  below opt out:

    - allow-unsigned-executable-memory: the one llvmlite actually needs
      (classic mmap(PROT_EXEC) JIT).
    - allow-jit: allows MAP_JIT; included as the standard pairing for
      numba apps (matches PyInstaller's recommendation).

  This plist REPLACES pyappdist's built-in default (which is only
  disable-library-validation), so that key must stay: without it the
  hardened python cannot load third-party wheels' .so/.dylib files, which
  are signed ad-hoc or by other identities.

  All three are permitted for Developer ID distribution and pass
  notarization without extra approval.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
